IMPORTANT THIRD-PARTY LICENSE REQUIREMENTS:

The epigenetic clock algorithms implemented in this software are based on 
methods developed at the University of California, San Diego (UCSD) and 
other institutions. Commercial use requires separate licensing.

PATENTED TECHNOLOGIES (UCSD):
-----------------------------
The following epigenetic clocks are patented by UCSD and require licensing 
for commercial applications:

1. Horvath Multi-tissue Clock (DNAmAge)
   - US Patent 9,938,579
   - 353 CpG sites, pan-tissue applicability
   - Inventor: Steve Horvath, PhD, ScD

2. GrimAge Clock
   - UCSD Technology Transfer Office
   - 1,030 CpG sites, mortality prediction
   - Lu AT, et al. (2019) Aging 11:303-327

3. PhenoAge Clock
   - UCSD/UCLA Technology Transfer
   - 513 CpG sites, 9 clinical biomarkers
   - Levine ME, et al. (2018) Aging 10:573-591

4. SkinBloodClock
   - UCSD Technology Transfer Office
   - Skin and blood optimized

5. DunedinPACE
   - Duke University / Columbia University
   - Pace of aging measurement
   - Belsky DW, et al. (2022) eLife 11:e73420

LICENSE TYPES:
